AI Factory — Project Roadmap
============================
Last updated: 2026-04-12

This file tracks the delta between the project vision (CLAUDE.md) and the current
implementation. Items are organized by priority. Nothing here is aspirational fluff —
every item maps to a specific gap found in the code.

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 CRITICAL — Security / Data Integrity
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

[x] Console log cleanup — api.js
    Removed console.log from request interceptor and success response interceptor.
    Only console.error remains (for failed requests). Responses visible in DevTools
    Network tab as intended; no data leaks to browser console on success.

[x] 401 Interceptor on Frontend
    frontend/src/utils/api.js — Response interceptor now detects 401, clears
    aif_token / aif_user / aif_avatar from localStorage, dispatches a custom
    'aif:session-expired' DOM event. Dashboard.jsx listens for the event, sets
    sessionExpired state, and redirects to /login after 3 s. ChatThread shows a
    lockout banner and disables the input/send button immediately on expiry.

[x] Protect Unauthenticated Routes
    All four routes now require Depends(get_current_user) + ownership checks:
      - GET  /conversations/{id}             → auth + _get_owned_conversation
      - POST /conversations/{id}/reopen      → auth + _get_owned_conversation
      - POST /conversations/{id}/decline-tasking → auth + _get_owned_conversation
      - GET  /agents/{conversation_id}/tickets   → auth + _get_owned_conversation
    Decision: full protection on all routes. Polling (GET /tickets) was intentionally
    open before but the cost of a small auth overhead is worth the security gain.
    Ownership is checked via Idea.user_id join (Conversation.user_id is not always set).
    Documented in CLAUDE.md §21.

[x] ALTER TABLE guard for project_tags column
    backend/main.py — Added ALTER TABLE guard:
      ALTER TABLE conversations ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS project_tags JSON
    Also fixed Conversation creation in conversations.py to always populate user_id
    (was always null, forcing the Idea-join ownership check on every auth route).
    Frontend: projectTags flows Dashboard → ChatThread as a prop; a project-type
    badge (Full-Stack / Backend API / Script / etc.) appears in the chat header
    once the PM agent has stamped tags after tasking.

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 HIGH — PM Agent Behavior & Quality
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

[x] PM Agent: Explicit Scope-Adaptive Ticket Count Instructions
    backend/agents/pm_agent.py — Phase 1 now instructs the PM to detect scope tier
    from the opening message before asking questions. Ticket generation rules now
    have explicit tiers replacing the vague "Aim for 6-12" line:
      Tier 1 (script/CLI):       1–2 questions, 1–3 tickets
      Tier 2 (backend/API):      3–5 questions, 4–8 tickets
      Tier 3 (full-stack):       5–8 questions, 8–15 tickets
    Also clarifies that Foundation/Core/Polish split is only required for Tier 3.

[x] PM Agent: Classify Project Type Early in Discovery
    frontend/src/pages/Dashboard.jsx + Dashboard.scss — Five project type chips
    (Web App, Backend API, Script/CLI, Mobile App, DevOps Tool) added to the New
    Idea panel. Clicking a chip embeds a [PROJECT_TYPE: X] prefix in the first
    message. Selecting the same chip again deselects (toggle). Chips disabled
    when Jira is not connected or no project is selected.
    backend/agents/pm_agent.py — Added "Pre-selected project type" section: when
    the [PROJECT_TYPE: X] tag is present, PM acknowledges it in the first line,
    sets scope tier from the tag, and skips the type question entirely. Added
    "Type mismatch detection" section: if conversation reveals a clear mismatch,
    PM explains why and asks to confirm before switching — never changes silently.

[ ] Developer Plan as Named Artifact
    backend/agents/pm_agent.py — The CLAUDE.md vision describes the PM producing
    a "developer plan" (tech stack, folder structure, libraries, tools, agent types
    needed) before generating tickets. Currently Phase 1 gathers this implicitly
    but it's not surfaced as a distinct structured output. Consider adding a
    "projectPlan" object to the ticket JSON that captures:
      - techStack: { backend, frontend, database, tools }
      - folderStructure: string description
      - externalServices: list
      - agentTypesNeeded: list (e.g. ["backend", "frontend"])
    This would make the PM output more useful as documentation and allow the
    generated CLAUDE.md to be richer and more accurate.

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 HIGH — Feature Gaps
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

[ ] Register Page: Personality Preference Not Stored
    frontend/src/pages/Register.jsx — Step 2 of the registration wizard captures
    a personality preference (concise / balanced / detailed) but it is never sent
    to the backend. The UserSettings model has no personality column. Either:
      Option A: Add personality column to UserSettings, send it on register, and
                use it to adjust the PM Agent's response style (e.g. shorter/longer
                replies in discovery).
      Option B: Remove the UI step until Option A is ready.
    Currently it's a broken promise to the user — they pick a preference that
    does nothing.

[ ] Email Notifications: Toggle Exists, Nothing Sends
    backend/models/user_settings.py — notifications_enabled is stored. There is
    no email sending logic anywhere. Either wire up a transactional email provider
    (SendGrid, Resend, etc.) or remove the toggle from the settings UI until ready.

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 MEDIUM — Agent System Expansion (Tag-Driven)
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    The project type tag system (has_frontend, has_backend, is_script,
    is_mobile_app, is_devops_program) is already plumbed end-to-end, but only
    two agent types exist. The following agents need to be built when their
    tag categories are common enough to warrant it:

[ ] Script / CLI Agent (is_script: true)
    Currently script tickets fall through to the Backend Developer Agent, which
    works but produces Node.js/Express scaffolding even for Python scripts.
    Need: backend/agents/script_agent.py + backend/services/script_agent.py
    Routing: agent_runner.run_ticket() should detect is_script and route
    accordingly. Script agent should default to Python and produce flat file
    structures, no server framework.

[ ] Mobile Developer Agent (is_mobile_app: true)
    Need: backend/agents/mobile_agent.py + backend/services/mobile_agent.py
    Default stack: React Native + Expo. CI/CD workflow should skip GitHub Pages
    (mobile apps don't deploy there) and optionally add an Expo build step.

[ ] DevOps Agent (is_devops_program: true)
    Need: backend/agents/devops_agent.py + backend/services/devops_agent.py
    Default output: Dockerfiles, GitHub Actions workflows, Terraform/K8s configs.
    No frontend, no GitHub Pages deploy.

[ ] Agent Routing in agent_runner.run_ticket()
    backend/services/agent_runner.py — Currently routes on ticket.type
    ("backend" | "frontend"). As new agent types are added, expand routing logic
    to also check project tags or a new ticket.agent_type field. Decision needed:
    derive agent from ticket type alone, or add explicit agent_type field to Ticket.

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 MEDIUM — Architecture & Developer Experience
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

[ ] WebSocket Support for Real-Time Agent Progress
    Currently all dev-agent progress updates use REST polling at ~1s intervals
    (frontend/src/components/ChatThread.jsx). This creates ~60 requests/min per
    active build. Replace with WebSocket or Server-Sent Events so the server
    pushes ticket status changes instead of the client polling.
    High impact: reduces server load, improves UX responsiveness.

[ ] Alembic Migrations
    backend/main.py — Schema changes are applied via hand-written ALTER TABLE
    guards. This is fragile as columns multiply. Add Alembic so that:
      - All schema changes are versioned
      - Rolling back a broken deploy is possible
      - Dev and prod can safely diverge and converge

[ ] Agent Output Inspection UI
    backend/models/ticket.py — Ticket.agent_output stores raw JSON from the dev
    agent but there's no UI to view it. Failed tickets show an error_msg but
    debugging requires direct DB access. Add a "view agent output" expandable
    panel in DevProgress.jsx for failed tickets.

[ ] Rate Limiting Per User
    backend/api/routes/agents.py — A single user can queue unlimited agent jobs.
    With no rate limiting, one user could exhaust LLM budget or lock up background
    workers. Add a simple per-user concurrency check: reject if the user already
    has a conversation in "processing" status.

[ ] LLM Cost Tracking
    No LLM usage is metered or capped. Track input/output tokens per conversation
    (Anthropic SDK returns usage in the response). Store on Ticket or Conversation.
    Surface in UI or admin dashboard. This is important before any public launch.

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 LOW — Polish & UX
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

[ ] Jira Project Auto-Creation
    backend/services/jira_service.py — Code for auto-creating a Jira project
    exists but is commented out in conversations.py. Users currently must pre-
    create their Jira project and select it. Re-enable auto-creation with a
    sensible fallback: if project_key already exists in the user's workspace,
    reuse it; otherwise create it.

[ ] Idea Title Auto-Derivation
    backend/models/idea.py — The Idea.title column exists (nullable) but is
    never populated. The History tab shows ideas without titles. Derive a short
    title (via LLM or simple truncation) from the first user message and store it
    when the conversation is created.

[ ] Empty State: History Tab with No Ideas
    frontend/src/pages/Dashboard.jsx — Check whether the History tab shows a
    meaningful empty state when the user has no ideas, or just an empty list.

[ ] JWT Expiry: User-Facing Feedback
    Related to the 401 interceptor item above. When the session expires and the
    user is redirected to /login, show a toast or message explaining why
    ("Your session expired — please log in again") rather than a blank redirect.

[ ] Conversation Ownership on Reopen/Decline Routes
    Even after adding auth to reopen/decline-tasking routes, add an ownership
    check: verify conversation.user_id matches the authenticated user's ID.
    Without this, authenticated users can still manipulate other users' conversations
    if they know the conversation ID.

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 DONE — Implemented and Verified
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

